I'm fairly new to this game myself, but I have managed to get past the
starving-every-game phase.

Here's a few things that I found helpful:
 - Don't waste too many moves. You don't have to completely clear a
level before moving down, and you can always come back. So if you are
short on food, don't spend too much time searching for secret passages
that may or may not be there; you'll cover more ground (and hence have
a better chance of finding some food) if you just move down to the
next level.
 - Learn which corpses you can eat, and which you can't. Learn which
things will rot, and which will not. Save the food that doesn't rot
for when you start getting hungry.
 - Learn to pray at the right times.

I guess that's about all I can say before I start giving spoilers. In
fact, that's about all I know about it anyway.

